# `fun.dll` Embedding Runtime License

**English** (this file) · [简体中文](LICENSE.dll.zh.md)

## Special Notice

`fun.dll` is the embedded runtime library of the Fun language. It allows third-party applications to integrate Fun scripts into their own processes as an extension language.

### 1. Free use (MIT license, no payment required)

You may use `fun.dll` free of charge in the following scenarios:

- Personal learning, research, and prototype development
- Internal tools and automation scripts (not distributed externally)
- Products released under an **open-source license (GPL/BSD/MIT, etc.)**, provided that the source code or binary of `fun.dll` is also open-sourced
- Non-commercial educational or academic projects

### 2. Commercial license (purchase required)

If you embed `fun.dll` into your own commercial product, and:

- The product is distributed **closed-source** (such as exe, dmg, apk, etc.); or
- The product is delivered as a **SaaS service** whose backend uses `fun.dll` as a core logic component; or
- You modify the source code of `fun.dll` and release it closed-source;

then you must purchase a commercial license. Please contact:

 zwd@funlang.org

### 3. Pricing and terms

The commercial license is a **one-time license**, priced per project or per company, and provides:

- Perpetual usage rights (current version)
- Prioritized technical support
- Customized modification services (optional)

Please inquire about the specific fees by email.

---

> **In simple terms**: If you integrate `fun.dll` into your software as a "glue" component and sell that software to customers, then please pay. All other cases are free.
